{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>נחית</b> — two times in the Masorah: נחית בחסדך, נחית כצאן עמך. Just as the shepherd pastures the sheep, each one according to the pasture suited to it, so the cloud guided them, each one according to his pace — the great one according to his greatness and the small one according to his smallness. And just as the shepherd rests the sheep at noon so that the heat and sun do not strike them, so they were encompassed by clouds so that the heat and sun would not strike them." "<b>עם זו</b> — three times in the Masorah. One is this one; and the others: עם זו קנית, עם זו יצרתי לי. This people You acquired — when You redeemed them; and as though You created them then as a new creation."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:13:03.448626693Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}